1
00:00:05,801 --> 00:00:07,300
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,325 --> 00:00:08,793
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:09,975 --> 00:00:11,042
I said go.

4
00:00:11,042 --> 00:00:12,744
(Episode 27)

5
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:16,133
Who do you think you are?
You're a criminal.

6
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:17,627
Criminal?

7
00:00:18,219 --> 00:00:19,783
Who's a criminal?

8
00:00:19,808 --> 00:00:21,610
Did you see me commit a crime?

9
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,215
I didn't see it, but I heard about it.

10
00:00:24,302 --> 00:00:27,747
If you wanted to con people,
do it yourself. Why drag my dad into it?

11
00:00:27,926 --> 00:00:30,559
Do you know what kind of situation
my dad's in because of you?

12
00:00:32,474 --> 00:00:33,738
Who are you?

13
00:00:35,947 --> 00:00:39,923
I'm the real daughter of Mr. Jang Hun Tae.

14
00:00:39,987 --> 00:00:41,070
So what?

15
00:00:45,521 --> 00:00:49,510
I've never seen a lowlife
as shameless as you in my life.

16
00:00:50,188 --> 00:00:53,397
Of all people, how could you go
to the man your mom remarried...

17
00:00:53,918 --> 00:00:55,332
You're not right in the head, are you?

18
00:00:55,553 --> 00:00:57,655
How did a lunatic like you
get a medical license?

19
00:00:57,756 --> 00:00:59,257
Did you con your way into that too?

20
00:01:03,615 --> 00:01:06,977
If he's my mom's husband, he's my dad too.

21
00:01:07,432 --> 00:01:08,466
What?

22
00:01:08,673 --> 00:01:11,409
If my mom remarried,
he's my dad, obviously.

23
00:01:11,929 --> 00:01:17,068
Unbelievable.

24
00:01:18,202 --> 00:01:22,773
You have everything and more than enough.

25
00:01:23,448 --> 00:01:26,684
And you can't even do that much for me?

26
00:01:27,459 --> 00:01:32,734
You stole our mom, and you and your dad
got all the love we should've gotten,

27
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:33,925
and you can't even do that one thing?

28
00:01:34,099 --> 00:01:35,855
Did we steal her?

29
00:01:35,987 --> 00:01:39,223
A good woman like her must've had
her reasons to leave her husband and kids.

30
00:01:39,270 --> 00:01:40,738
Did I kick her out?

31
00:01:40,885 --> 00:01:42,922
Why take it out on me
for what my dad did wrong?

32
00:01:42,947 --> 00:01:45,103
What? Forget it.

33
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:49,307
We'd be here all night arguing this out,
so you fix this.

34
00:01:49,474 --> 00:01:51,743
Make sure your rotten in-laws
can't touch my dad,

35
00:01:51,743 --> 00:01:54,116
that they can't come
anywhere near my family,

36
00:01:54,292 --> 00:01:57,881
and that we don't get dragged
into the mud. You stop them!

37
00:02:08,853 --> 00:02:11,183
How did it go, Doctor?

38
00:02:12,149 --> 00:02:17,367
She's a doctor who specializes
in memory loss.

39
00:02:17,392 --> 00:02:21,122
There's a way to cure her, isn't there?

40
00:02:23,028 --> 00:02:25,081
No. There isn't.

41
00:02:25,543 --> 00:02:29,814
She's completely lost it.
There's no cure for this patient.

42
00:02:30,301 --> 00:02:32,704
What do we do?

43
00:02:32,884 --> 00:02:36,411
She has her whole life ahead of her.
What do we do?

44
00:02:36,436 --> 00:02:40,322
Please help us, Doctor.

45
00:02:40,439 --> 00:02:41,640
Doctor!

46
00:02:41,665 --> 00:02:44,002
What did the doctor say?

47
00:02:44,027 --> 00:02:45,696
She didn't figure out
you're faking, did she?

48
00:02:47,691 --> 00:02:49,426
Doctor, my foot.

49
00:02:51,568 --> 00:02:53,917
She's a con artist too,
come to think of it.

50
00:02:54,739 --> 00:02:57,443
What are you talking about?
Make it make sense.

51
00:02:57,749 --> 00:02:59,951
That girl who just left isn't a doctor,

52
00:02:59,976 --> 00:03:03,046
she's a con artist who lied to Su Nam
so she could see me.

53
00:03:04,075 --> 00:03:05,676
What?

54
00:03:08,372 --> 00:03:10,927
Did that jerk Seong Uk send her
to mess with you?

55
00:03:11,809 --> 00:03:15,753
What did those people threaten
the Chairman with?

56
00:03:23,754 --> 00:03:27,058
I've made up my mind, Heung Sik.

57
00:03:28,479 --> 00:03:32,106
For making her lose her memory like that,

58
00:03:33,724 --> 00:03:36,928
I'm going to turn myself in
and say it was all me.

59
00:03:37,455 --> 00:03:43,589
I'll turn myself in and tell her family
to get her proper care at a big hospital,

60
00:03:44,102 --> 00:03:46,358
so you pretend you don't know.
Stay out of it.

61
00:03:46,383 --> 00:03:47,784
Wait a minute.

62
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:50,948
Why would you say you did what I did, Mom?

63
00:03:51,055 --> 00:03:53,138
If anyone turns himself in,
it should be me.

64
00:03:53,198 --> 00:03:56,801
Is that so? Then you go turn yourself in.

65
00:03:57,148 --> 00:04:00,785
I'll bring you food in prison.
I won't miss a single day.

66
00:04:01,911 --> 00:04:03,018
Mom.

67
00:04:05,222 --> 00:04:08,696
You rotten kid!

68
00:04:11,383 --> 00:04:14,977
If my own kid is precious,
so is everyone else's.

69
00:04:16,273 --> 00:04:18,930
Her family has no idea...

70
00:04:18,955 --> 00:04:21,490
that she's ended up like that.

71
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:25,916
Was she just any smart kid?

72
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:29,407
She's a doctor who made it
through tough years of studying abroad...

73
00:04:29,534 --> 00:04:32,407
We turned her soft in the head,

74
00:04:32,554 --> 00:04:36,228
and we're just sitting here shamelessly.
Is that any way for a person to act?

75
00:04:36,253 --> 00:04:39,891
We're no better than animals.
We're beasts!

76
00:04:43,588 --> 00:04:47,126
I can't breathe, and I can't sleep.

77
00:04:47,270 --> 00:04:51,740
This is pure torture. What are we doing?

78
00:04:59,243 --> 00:05:02,880
I have a son named Gyeol.

79
00:05:05,069 --> 00:05:08,873
I love Mu Jin as much as I love Gyeol.

80
00:05:10,821 --> 00:05:15,660
If Gyeol is facing hardship,
I'll take the lead.

81
00:05:16,888 --> 00:05:22,046
If Gyeol is happy, I'll watch from behind.

82
00:05:26,844 --> 00:05:28,846
That's how I love...

83
00:05:30,668 --> 00:05:32,570
Mu Jin.

84
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:38,152
From now on,

85
00:05:38,929 --> 00:05:42,933
I will never be the first
to let go of Mu Jin's hand.

86
00:05:46,390 --> 00:05:48,016
I'm sorry.

87
00:05:54,210 --> 00:05:58,638
She loves Mu Jin like her own son?

88
00:05:59,023 --> 00:06:03,828
So what, I don't love my own son?

89
00:06:03,935 --> 00:06:06,683
Is she saying I'm not even a mother?

90
00:06:07,057 --> 00:06:09,134
I don't think that's what she means.

91
00:06:09,627 --> 00:06:14,435
I think she means she loves Mu Jin
as deeply as her own son...

92
00:06:14,938 --> 00:06:18,679
Hey. Did you get hired
as Han Gyu Rim's spokesperson?

93
00:06:20,845 --> 00:06:24,826
She says she'll never be the first
to let go of Mu Jin's hand.

94
00:06:24,851 --> 00:06:27,648
Is that a declaration of war?
How dare she?

95
00:06:28,826 --> 00:06:30,084
She doesn't back down.

96
00:06:30,116 --> 00:06:34,194
No matter how hard I stomp on her,
she's tougher than a weed.

97
00:06:34,518 --> 00:06:39,879
And she still fires back
with every word she wants to say.

98
00:06:41,178 --> 00:06:45,165
Parasite, maggot, cockroach, leech.

99
00:06:46,437 --> 00:06:48,193
You said that to her, Mom?

100
00:06:48,218 --> 00:06:50,687
I did, and she has no shame at all.

101
00:06:50,821 --> 00:06:53,491
She doesn't seem to feel humiliated
or even hurt.

102
00:06:53,937 --> 00:06:56,573
Talk about thick-skinned.

103
00:06:57,090 --> 00:07:01,130
If they're crazy about each other,
if they're madly in love,

104
00:07:01,155 --> 00:07:02,730
can't you just leave them alone?

105
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,056
You promised you would, Mom.

106
00:07:05,189 --> 00:07:07,405
Love, my foot.

107
00:07:07,871 --> 00:07:11,077
What kind of love is so crazy
you'd die for it?

108
00:07:11,476 --> 00:07:12,730
Hey, Kim Yun Jin.

109
00:07:12,755 --> 00:07:15,324
If you side with that girl one more time,

110
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:18,674
I'll throw you out penniless too!

111
00:07:18,699 --> 00:07:22,765
Isn't there some kind of
dictionary of curse words?

112
00:07:38,089 --> 00:07:39,590
You're cute.

113
00:07:40,598 --> 00:07:43,232
Let's save the romance for after work.

114
00:07:43,989 --> 00:07:45,496
No.

115
00:07:48,292 --> 00:07:50,194
At a time like this,

116
00:07:50,654 --> 00:07:52,211
get it together, Chef.

117
00:07:52,236 --> 00:07:54,272
This is no time to slack off.

118
00:07:55,619 --> 00:07:59,223
Then stop being so pretty.

119
00:08:01,679 --> 00:08:03,481
Wash your eyes with this.

120
00:08:04,048 --> 00:08:05,583
What's pretty about me?

121
00:08:05,929 --> 00:08:07,831
You've obviously never seen
a really pretty girl.

122
00:08:08,079 --> 00:08:10,348
But what are you, really?

123
00:08:10,607 --> 00:08:13,174
How can you look this pretty
even with foam on your face?

124
00:08:14,553 --> 00:08:16,480
You had a latte?

125
00:08:16,655 --> 00:08:21,447
- Must've been good.
- I said wash your eyes with this, mister.

126
00:08:21,705 --> 00:08:23,409
Merry Christmas.

127
00:08:25,132 --> 00:08:26,557
Stop it!

128
00:08:32,604 --> 00:08:34,491
I've lived as hard as I possibly could.

129
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:39,038
Being poor isn't my fault, Mu Jin.

130
00:08:40,137 --> 00:08:43,596
From now on, I'm going to be a bad person.

131
00:08:44,482 --> 00:08:47,506
I'll stop worrying about knowing my place,

132
00:08:48,012 --> 00:08:51,009
and be pushy and shameless.

133
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:55,619
After all the love you have given me.

134
00:09:05,329 --> 00:09:06,969
Keep your promise.

135
00:09:09,206 --> 00:09:11,255
Promise me you won't let go...

136
00:09:12,183 --> 00:09:16,230
of my hand first. Keep that promise.

137
00:09:19,123 --> 00:09:23,812
Then I'll keep my promise never to lose,

138
00:09:24,715 --> 00:09:29,104
my promise to win, no matter what.

139
00:09:50,341 --> 00:09:53,177
Even if the whole world criticizes
and curses me,

140
00:09:53,577 --> 00:09:57,982
I'll be even more open
and proud about my love.

141
00:10:07,151 --> 00:10:08,226
No way.

142
00:10:08,251 --> 00:10:09,340
(Sister-in-law, Groom Han Gyu O and
Bride Kwon Hui Na Got Married)

143
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:11,142
You're the first to know, brother-in-law.

144
00:10:11,421 --> 00:10:12,523
Congratulate us.

145
00:10:13,210 --> 00:10:14,311
That's crazy.

146
00:10:18,589 --> 00:10:20,457
You got married, Gyu O?

147
00:10:21,558 --> 00:10:23,160
Did Hui Na tell you?

148
00:10:31,455 --> 00:10:35,105
- What's that?
- It means shocked, surprised, and happy.

149
00:10:36,753 --> 00:10:38,088
Congratulations, Gyu O.

150
00:10:38,113 --> 00:10:39,850
I'm so happy for you.

151
00:10:41,184 --> 00:10:44,799
I'll tell them when the time is right,
so keep it from the family for now.

152
00:10:45,883 --> 00:10:47,656
Got it.

153
00:10:49,967 --> 00:10:51,335
Has the bruise faded a bit?

154
00:10:52,101 --> 00:10:53,868
I told the family it's pink eye.

155
00:10:54,452 --> 00:10:56,554
When are you going to name
the guy who hit you?

156
00:10:57,251 --> 00:10:59,229
I told you, no one hit me.

157
00:10:59,443 --> 00:11:01,011
I got hit by a baseball bat.

158
00:11:03,935 --> 00:11:05,465
You think I'm stupid?

159
00:11:06,049 --> 00:11:08,121
I pretended to buy it,
and you think you really fooled me?

160
00:11:09,115 --> 00:11:10,506
You were pretending?

161
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:12,600
You've got a week to tell me who hit you.

162
00:11:13,076 --> 00:11:14,897
Before I go looking for him myself.

163
00:11:16,019 --> 00:11:17,792
Have a great life with Hui Na, Gyu O.

164
00:11:18,375 --> 00:11:21,995
Be so happy that the whole world
cries tears of envy.

165
00:11:22,439 --> 00:11:23,807
Don't change the subject.

166
00:11:24,115 --> 00:11:25,883
I'm not changing the subject.

167
00:11:26,997 --> 00:11:29,075
I really want you to be happy.

168
00:11:29,353 --> 00:11:32,389
There should be a law that you
and Gyu Rim get to be happy.

169
00:11:36,361 --> 00:11:38,326
So this is the wedding ring.

170
00:11:38,695 --> 00:11:41,691
- It's totally killer.
- Awesome, right?

171
00:11:43,808 --> 00:11:46,217
What's this?

172
00:12:00,885 --> 00:12:03,454
(Seo Min Ju)

173
00:12:05,590 --> 00:12:06,891
Open the door!

174
00:12:22,273 --> 00:12:24,542
That gigolo who seduced my mom.

175
00:12:24,942 --> 00:12:28,612
The guy you were on the phone with,
that's Han Gyu O, right?

176
00:12:29,714 --> 00:12:30,852
No.

177
00:12:32,383 --> 00:12:35,252
That's why you stood Han Gyu O up
and avoided him at first.

178
00:12:35,511 --> 00:12:36,587
No.

179
00:12:36,654 --> 00:12:39,023
And that's why you freaked out
and tried to stop me and Han Gyu O.

180
00:12:41,325 --> 00:12:45,513
I didn't think the pieces
would fall into place this easily.

181
00:12:45,763 --> 00:12:47,965
I think you're misunderstanding something.

182
00:12:48,498 --> 00:12:51,038
Han Gyu O isn't a gigolo.

183
00:12:52,436 --> 00:12:54,923
You think I came here to ask you
because I don't know that?

184
00:12:56,273 --> 00:12:58,442
I'm here to put the final nail
in your coffin today.

185
00:12:59,019 --> 00:13:01,679
- Min Ju.
- Where's Han Gyu O right now?

186
00:13:03,047 --> 00:13:05,516
My mom really wants to see Han Gyu O.

187
00:13:06,584 --> 00:13:08,707
- Where is that jerk?
- Hey!

188
00:13:10,307 --> 00:13:12,142
I changed my strategy.

189
00:13:13,124 --> 00:13:15,693
I'm going to get on my mom's good side,

190
00:13:15,953 --> 00:13:19,415
and be her perfect little darling
so I get her whole inheritance.

191
00:13:19,897 --> 00:13:21,423
So where's Han Gyu O?

192
00:13:22,152 --> 00:13:24,283
I have to go to work. Please leave.

193
00:13:28,219 --> 00:13:31,103
He didn't just vanish into thin air,

194
00:13:31,315 --> 00:13:33,538
but Su Chan and Yun Gi
say they don't know anything.

195
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:36,244
Where is Han Gyu O?

196
00:13:44,789 --> 00:13:47,705
- What?
- See this wedding ring?

197
00:13:48,639 --> 00:13:51,141
I married Gyu O.

198
00:13:52,376 --> 00:13:55,713
Are you insane? Are you messing with me?

199
00:13:55,872 --> 00:13:58,253
Who jokes about marriage?

200
00:13:58,622 --> 00:14:04,475
Yesterday, I married him
in front of my grandparents,

201
00:14:05,382 --> 00:14:09,716
and now he's my husband,
and anyone who messes with my husband,

202
00:14:09,847 --> 00:14:14,527
no matter who they are
or where they stand, I'll crush them all.

203
00:14:14,552 --> 00:14:16,067
You've really lost your mind.

204
00:14:16,092 --> 00:14:18,502
You and your mom are the crazy ones.

205
00:14:20,697 --> 00:14:23,533
I doubt there's any friendship
left between us,

206
00:14:24,461 --> 00:14:27,865
but if there's even a speck left,
I'm asking you.

207
00:14:29,406 --> 00:14:32,375
Please leave my Gyu O alone.

208
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:44,214
Mom, what do we do?

209
00:14:44,654 --> 00:14:47,724
Han Gyu O married Kwon Hui Na!

210
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:03,817
Gyeol, just hypothetically,

211
00:15:06,791 --> 00:15:10,098
what would you think if I were
your homeroom teacher's boyfriend?

212
00:15:10,907 --> 00:15:12,475
I'd be so mad.

213
00:15:12,609 --> 00:15:15,232
Last time, you asked me
for my teacher's name too.

214
00:15:16,761 --> 00:15:19,222
Gyu O, why do you keep bugging my teacher?

215
00:15:19,977 --> 00:15:22,679
You really like Ms. Kwon, don't you?

216
00:15:22,913 --> 00:15:26,145
If your favorite teacher and Gyu O
became close friends,

217
00:15:26,266 --> 00:15:28,012
wouldn't that make you even happier?

218
00:15:28,037 --> 00:15:31,805
No. Ms. Kwon is going to marry me someday.

219
00:15:37,027 --> 00:15:39,845
Why would you marry your homeroom teacher?

220
00:15:39,870 --> 00:15:41,271
How old are you?

221
00:15:41,296 --> 00:15:43,115
And what about Da Som?

222
00:15:45,308 --> 00:15:47,544
You made it clear back then too, Gyu O.

223
00:15:47,857 --> 00:15:51,266
You said you didn't want to mix
personal and professional.

224
00:15:51,868 --> 00:15:54,337
That was then.
You never know who you'll end up with.

225
00:15:54,471 --> 00:15:56,640
Anyway, I'm totally against it.

226
00:15:56,767 --> 00:16:00,533
Gyu O, don't like my teacher. Ever.

227
00:16:01,071 --> 00:16:02,760
Thanks for the meal.

228
00:16:14,439 --> 00:16:17,442
My legs hurt. It's been a while.

229
00:16:25,149 --> 00:16:27,862
I heard everything from here.

230
00:16:28,258 --> 00:16:30,557
Are you and Gyu O in a love triangle?

231
00:16:30,674 --> 00:16:32,109
No.

232
00:16:32,596 --> 00:16:35,866
Right. Family shouldn't do that.

233
00:16:37,168 --> 00:16:39,085
Gyu O is really weird.

234
00:16:39,110 --> 00:16:41,222
He said he likes someone else.

235
00:16:42,319 --> 00:16:45,923
That's why staying loyal is so hard.

236
00:16:46,108 --> 00:16:49,373
Look what happened to Jeong Mong Ju.
Yi Bang Won had him killed!

237
00:16:49,398 --> 00:16:53,457
Hey, when I think about that,
your mom's really something.

238
00:16:53,757 --> 00:16:56,059
She's all in on Kim Mu Jin.

239
00:16:56,561 --> 00:16:58,097
Mu Jin too.

240
00:16:58,608 --> 00:17:04,247
He said he's liked Mom every minute
since the day they first met.

241
00:17:05,409 --> 00:17:08,761
How can you trust what a guy says?

242
00:17:09,186 --> 00:17:13,651
Even after you grow up,
let's not get tangled up with family.

243
00:17:14,478 --> 00:17:17,947
I hate the idea of marrying into
the same family twice.

244
00:17:18,636 --> 00:17:21,557
Okay. But...

245
00:17:21,692 --> 00:17:24,674
I liked Ms. Kwon first.

246
00:17:24,699 --> 00:17:26,141
Before anyone else in my class, too.

247
00:17:26,323 --> 00:17:27,624
Is that so?

248
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:31,630
You heard him, right? Gyeol was first.

249
00:17:32,235 --> 00:17:35,672
Gyu O, go find someone else.

250
00:17:35,981 --> 00:17:37,201
Happy?

251
00:17:39,416 --> 00:17:40,717
Knees behind toes.

252
00:17:46,724 --> 00:17:47,822
Eat.

253
00:17:54,612 --> 00:17:57,817
- Gyu Yeong's staying with Su Nam, right?
- Yeah.

254
00:17:58,041 --> 00:18:00,177
I'll go see her after school.

255
00:18:01,252 --> 00:18:02,753
Good idea.

256
00:18:03,166 --> 00:18:05,502
She must be lonely and lost,
struggling at someone else's house.

257
00:18:06,103 --> 00:18:07,470
Help her out if you can.

258
00:18:07,495 --> 00:18:11,052
What? I'm going to make her
pay your medical bills.

259
00:18:11,354 --> 00:18:14,665
Are you soft tofu? The ultimate sucker?
Don't you have any pride?

260
00:18:14,711 --> 00:18:18,799
After how Han Gyu Yeong treated us,
you want to help that psycho?

261
00:18:18,824 --> 00:18:20,492
Forget it. Just don't go.

262
00:18:21,191 --> 00:18:22,979
Let's pretend I never told you
about Gyu Yeong.

263
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:27,462
How'd you turn out to be such a softie?
You don't get it from Dad.

264
00:18:27,487 --> 00:18:30,730
Dad's selfish and sly,
and he runs from any injustice.

265
00:18:30,848 --> 00:18:32,483
- Then Mom?
- Hey!

266
00:18:33,056 --> 00:18:35,600
No. Definitely not that woman.

267
00:18:35,625 --> 00:18:37,060
Don't even bring her up.

268
00:18:37,347 --> 00:18:38,941
Don't even say the M in Mom.

269
00:18:40,150 --> 00:18:43,632
Han Gyu Yeong was awful to us, though.

270
00:18:43,733 --> 00:18:46,903
In elementary school, I shook a tambourine
while she was studying for an exam,

271
00:18:46,934 --> 00:18:48,659
and she smacked me with it.

272
00:18:48,854 --> 00:18:50,333
She got you too.

273
00:18:50,358 --> 00:18:53,094
You got smacked for eating
all the ice cream she bought.

274
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:56,266
Maybe that's why we're both bad at school.
All those smacks back then.

275
00:18:56,291 --> 00:18:57,426
Forget it.

276
00:18:58,368 --> 00:19:00,361
My ear hurts. Stop.

277
00:19:00,731 --> 00:19:04,185
Now that I think about it,
Han Gyu Yeong was a total child abuser.

278
00:19:04,210 --> 00:19:05,980
We should report her to the police.

279
00:19:06,005 --> 00:19:07,778
Let's report her!

280
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:09,580
Han Gyu Yeong did that?

281
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:13,150
That viper bullied you and even hit you?

282
00:19:13,229 --> 00:19:15,876
Gyu Seo! What's this eye patch?

283
00:19:15,901 --> 00:19:17,770
Did she do this too?

284
00:19:18,168 --> 00:19:20,659
What are you doing?
Let's go to the police!

285
00:19:20,684 --> 00:19:22,347
Sure. Let's go to the police.

286
00:19:22,372 --> 00:19:25,198
I'll report you as a stalker,
so let's go to the police together, ma'am.

287
00:19:25,556 --> 00:19:30,227
As a fan,

288
00:19:30,337 --> 00:19:36,443
when I heard Gyu Seo and Gyu Min
were abused as kids, I just snapped.

289
00:19:36,468 --> 00:19:38,002
Why are you eavesdropping on us?

290
00:19:38,375 --> 00:19:40,577
Why do you keep secretly
following us around?

291
00:19:41,144 --> 00:19:43,408
What business is our family of yours,
you Misery-style stalker?

292
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:48,497
I just feel like you two are my own kids.

293
00:19:48,522 --> 00:19:51,139
- Out of pure fan love...
- Don't be my fan.

294
00:19:51,522 --> 00:19:53,634
I can't stand fans like you.

295
00:19:53,777 --> 00:19:56,852
If we catch you following us again,
we'll really call the police.

296
00:19:57,027 --> 00:19:58,428
This is your only warning.

297
00:19:59,068 --> 00:20:00,485
Gyu Seo!

298
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:01,899
Gyu Min.

299
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:06,432
- You understand how I feel, right?
- No. I don't.

300
00:20:06,576 --> 00:20:08,478
You know you're not normal either, right?

301
00:20:08,638 --> 00:20:10,438
Han Gyu Seo, wait up!

302
00:20:14,064 --> 00:20:17,432
My own kids don't even recognize me,
their own mom.

303
00:20:20,717 --> 00:20:24,746
Han Gyu Yeong has been nasty
since she was little.

304
00:20:25,101 --> 00:20:28,206
What did she do to my babies?

305
00:20:34,264 --> 00:20:37,648
- Can I come in?
- Yes.

306
00:20:40,596 --> 00:20:43,796
- Where are you going?
- To the Chairman.

307
00:20:44,008 --> 00:20:47,480
- The Chairman?
- My mom's new husband.

308
00:20:51,788 --> 00:20:53,723
Please come with me, Heung Sik.

309
00:20:54,171 --> 00:20:56,573
Should I? All right.

310
00:20:56,693 --> 00:20:59,897
From now on, wherever you go,
you go with me.

311
00:21:00,804 --> 00:21:04,080
But first, let go of my hand.

312
00:21:07,392 --> 00:21:08,732
Is there poop on my hand?

313
00:21:10,293 --> 00:21:12,469
No, it's not that.

314
00:21:13,237 --> 00:21:15,513
Stop being so touchy-feely with me.

315
00:21:15,538 --> 00:21:16,873
You're a grown woman, for crying out loud.

316
00:21:16,898 --> 00:21:18,786
What do you care?

317
00:21:18,909 --> 00:21:22,758
You said you'd pass even if someone
brought you a hundred truckloads of me.

318
00:21:22,783 --> 00:21:26,368
You said even a thousand,
ten thousand truckloads, no thanks.

319
00:21:26,850 --> 00:21:29,703
Well, that's true, of course.

320
00:21:31,128 --> 00:21:33,764
What are you two doing here?

321
00:21:37,707 --> 00:21:39,976
Have you gone back to being that vixen?

322
00:21:40,001 --> 00:21:41,881
No, it's not that.

323
00:21:42,002 --> 00:21:45,148
She just tried on her own clothes.

324
00:21:45,173 --> 00:21:47,186
Grandma, how do I look? Pretty, right?

325
00:21:47,257 --> 00:21:51,972
Yes. Pretty. As pretty as can be.

326
00:21:53,769 --> 00:21:56,652
You looked just like a vixen, so...

327
00:21:58,929 --> 00:22:00,703
What do we do?

328
00:22:00,811 --> 00:22:05,189
A bright girl like you,

329
00:22:05,447 --> 00:22:08,699
and look what we're doing to you.

330
00:22:10,046 --> 00:22:11,715
You said you'd turn yourself in.

331
00:22:13,034 --> 00:22:14,464
I will.

332
00:22:15,065 --> 00:22:18,702
I will, but let's talk again
after tonight.

333
00:22:18,702 --> 00:22:21,571
Forget it.
Stop talking and turn yourself in.

334
00:22:21,705 --> 00:22:25,565
We're accomplices,
so let's ask them to split the sentence.

335
00:22:25,682 --> 00:22:27,617
Let's go to the police now.

336
00:22:27,750 --> 00:22:29,579
Wait.

337
00:22:29,579 --> 00:22:31,043
- Wait.
- You rotten punk.

338
00:22:32,616 --> 00:22:34,284
Give me some time first.

339
00:22:34,785 --> 00:22:36,520
I've got something to do.

340
00:22:36,566 --> 00:22:40,484
What does a jobless bum
like you have to do all day?

341
00:22:42,328 --> 00:22:46,503
I've got something I need to get treated.

342
00:22:47,964 --> 00:22:49,766
Don't lie.

343
00:22:49,946 --> 00:22:53,754
Sick, my foot. You could take down an ox.

344
00:22:55,872 --> 00:22:58,175
- Hemorrhoids.
- Hemorrhoids?

345
00:22:59,309 --> 00:23:04,488
You know how damn painful that is, right?

346
00:23:04,895 --> 00:23:08,753
It's not like I'm going to run away.

347
00:23:08,812 --> 00:23:12,337
I'll turn myself in like you said
and come clean,

348
00:23:14,156 --> 00:23:17,593
so just give me one week until it heals.

349
00:23:18,661 --> 00:23:22,372
What kind of mother am I?
How did I not know about that?

350
00:23:22,397 --> 00:23:24,768
- How bad is it?
- Really bad.

351
00:23:24,799 --> 00:23:26,881
Show me. Hold still.

352
00:23:41,201 --> 00:23:44,743
- You met my Seo Hyeon?
- Yes.

353
00:23:46,934 --> 00:23:50,535
I didn't know they'd come
and threaten you too, sir.

354
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,461
I'm sorry for the trouble.

355
00:23:55,154 --> 00:23:59,762
So you left home and you're staying
at this man's place? Together?

356
00:24:00,022 --> 00:24:02,572
It's not that kind of relationship.

357
00:24:02,828 --> 00:24:04,980
My mother lives there too.

358
00:24:05,181 --> 00:24:10,516
Anyway, it's just a temporary shelter,
nothing more, nothing less.

359
00:24:10,695 --> 00:24:17,458
To be precise, I'm just a guy friend
of her sister, Gyu Rim.

360
00:24:17,575 --> 00:24:21,189
Those people won't just sit back.

361
00:24:21,548 --> 00:24:25,339
If you don't give them what they want,
they'll do something to hurt me.

362
00:24:28,393 --> 00:24:29,594
Please help me.

363
00:24:33,895 --> 00:24:37,790
You said I'm your daughter too.
Then act like a father.

364
00:24:37,835 --> 00:24:39,415
What are you saying?

365
00:24:40,115 --> 00:24:41,995
Didn't you come here to apologize?

366
00:24:42,114 --> 00:24:46,700
Don't just say I'm your daughter.
Show me what a real father does.

367
00:24:47,074 --> 00:24:51,666
You can easily handle lowlifes like that.

368
00:24:53,161 --> 00:24:56,777
Hey, even if you got on your knees
and begged, it wouldn't be enough,

369
00:24:56,802 --> 00:24:59,244
and now you want him
to take responsibility for what you did?

370
00:25:01,321 --> 00:25:04,436
Please try to understand.

371
00:25:04,608 --> 00:25:09,963
She's been backed into a corner,
so I think she's lost it a little.

372
00:25:10,462 --> 00:25:12,175
If word gets out about the sham marriage,

373
00:25:14,269 --> 00:25:18,789
if people find out it wasn't one-sided,
that it was a con on both sides,

374
00:25:20,222 --> 00:25:22,795
I'm finished in this field.

375
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:24,988
I can't fall apart like this.

376
00:25:25,568 --> 00:25:27,887
After everything it took to get here.

377
00:25:29,524 --> 00:25:31,748
- Gyu Yeong.
- Help me.

378
00:25:35,842 --> 00:25:37,534
Help you how?

379
00:25:39,175 --> 00:25:41,363
What those people want is money,

380
00:25:41,990 --> 00:25:46,477
so you want me to pay, settle,
and keep them quiet. Right?

381
00:25:47,515 --> 00:25:51,424
But I have no intention
of giving them any money.

382
00:25:52,149 --> 00:25:54,628
Not a single cent.

383
00:25:54,653 --> 00:25:56,002
Sir.

384
00:25:58,315 --> 00:25:59,783
Gyu Yeong.

385
00:26:00,543 --> 00:26:05,983
Keep being nice, and people start
thinking they're entitled to it.

386
00:26:08,154 --> 00:26:10,673
I hope you're not one of those people.

387
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:15,709
I'm sorry.

388
00:26:16,151 --> 00:26:19,157
I have a meeting in five minutes.
I must ask you to step outside.

389
00:26:36,661 --> 00:26:39,628
The phone is off.
You'll be connected to voicemail.

390
00:26:39,755 --> 00:26:42,202
After the beep, you will be charged.

391
00:26:44,067 --> 00:26:46,401
Han Gyu Yeong, it's me.

392
00:26:47,508 --> 00:26:51,282
Why do you keep your phone off
and make people worry?

393
00:26:52,255 --> 00:26:54,960
You didn't change your number
to cut ties with us, did you?

394
00:26:58,561 --> 00:27:02,702
Sorry for bugging you
after we agreed to cut ties,

395
00:27:04,376 --> 00:27:09,216
but if you're alive,
just send me a single dot to let me know.

396
00:27:10,615 --> 00:27:13,221
If you do that, I won't bother you again.

397
00:27:14,326 --> 00:27:16,279
Your message has been recorded.

398
00:27:20,821 --> 00:27:22,948
Why? Gyu Yeong...

399
00:27:23,589 --> 00:27:26,510
You can't reach your sister?

400
00:27:31,761 --> 00:27:37,662
If you give me her new address
or her work address, I'll go check on her.

401
00:27:37,793 --> 00:27:39,889
Whether she's alive or dead.

402
00:27:42,128 --> 00:27:44,915
She quit the hospital she worked at,

403
00:27:46,302 --> 00:27:48,082
and I don't even know her address.

404
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:51,920
I'm supposed to be her sister,
but I don't know a single thing.

405
00:27:52,257 --> 00:27:53,788
Some sister I am...

406
00:28:08,319 --> 00:28:09,810
Do one with me too.

407
00:28:12,988 --> 00:28:15,669
An interview, I mean. With me too.

408
00:28:23,581 --> 00:28:27,465
If you spread fake news and ran
my business into the ground,

409
00:28:27,991 --> 00:28:31,017
isn't giving me a chance to respond...

410
00:28:32,210 --> 00:28:35,021
what you call journalism?

411
00:28:35,833 --> 00:28:40,082
So you're Chef Kim Mu Jin.

412
00:28:40,941 --> 00:28:43,003
I've never reported fake news.

413
00:28:43,217 --> 00:28:46,302
So you're using your privilege
to bury the messenger?

414
00:28:46,662 --> 00:28:51,079
You know this is clearly press suppression
and intimidation, right?

415
00:28:51,104 --> 00:28:52,306
Privilege?

416
00:28:53,468 --> 00:28:55,644
I'm proposing a business deal.

417
00:28:56,835 --> 00:29:00,293
A few thousand in ad revenue
won't satisfy you either, will it?

418
00:29:00,318 --> 00:29:01,793
What are you talking about?

419
00:29:02,938 --> 00:29:04,538
If it were me...

420
00:29:04,655 --> 00:29:07,359
since you already took the dirty money,

421
00:29:08,620 --> 00:29:12,987
I'd go even bigger with this
and really pick a fight.

422
00:29:13,012 --> 00:29:16,052
- Hey, what money did I take?
- That way,

423
00:29:17,134 --> 00:29:20,841
the client who told you to frame me
will start sweating,

424
00:29:20,955 --> 00:29:22,815
and they'll pay you even more, won't they?

425
00:29:24,201 --> 00:29:29,214
I bet you could get three times
what you got paid this time.

426
00:29:29,634 --> 00:29:33,003
You want to get sued
for false accusation, punk?

427
00:29:33,348 --> 00:29:36,163
You know threatening a public figure
is aggravated intimidation, right?

428
00:29:39,828 --> 00:29:41,163
Hello, Jeong Woo.

429
00:29:42,263 --> 00:29:44,163
I don't think I'll do the interview.

430
00:29:44,590 --> 00:29:47,702
I suddenly don't feel like it.
I don't want to show my face either.

431
00:29:48,781 --> 00:29:53,056
Come to think of it,
it'd only be doing others a favor.

432
00:29:54,895 --> 00:29:56,157
What's this all of a sudden?

433
00:29:56,182 --> 00:30:01,250
Hey, man. Your family owns
the second-largest abalone farm in Wando.

434
00:30:02,162 --> 00:30:05,447
Let's just close the restaurant
and go harvest abalone in Wando.

435
00:30:05,907 --> 00:30:07,821
I'm serious.

436
00:30:08,135 --> 00:30:11,425
We can harvest kelp and seaweed too.
I'd be really good at it.

437
00:30:12,215 --> 00:30:15,722
Forget it. I'm not doing the interview.
I really can't do it.

438
00:30:15,955 --> 00:30:17,365
Just...

439
00:30:18,499 --> 00:30:22,492
Hey, it's not like we'll starve
if we close the restaurant.

440
00:30:22,924 --> 00:30:24,417
Let's go down to Wando.

441
00:30:24,941 --> 00:30:26,601
I'll be really good at harvesting abalone.

442
00:30:28,435 --> 00:30:32,433
Chef Kim Mu Jin, I hear you've prepared
something special for today?

443
00:30:33,087 --> 00:30:34,300
Yes.

444
00:30:34,444 --> 00:30:36,850
(Hidden Truth Behind the Da Solo Scandal,
Chef Kim Mu Jin Appears in Person!)

445
00:30:37,075 --> 00:30:42,399
Our purchase ledgers and all tax invoices
from the past three years.

446
00:30:44,928 --> 00:30:46,681
And the ingredients you claim I faked,

447
00:30:46,706 --> 00:30:51,401
their suppliers' contact info is included,
so go ahead and check.

448
00:30:52,494 --> 00:30:54,396
As for the food recycling claim,

449
00:30:54,617 --> 00:30:59,530
I'll release the raw, unedited footage
from our kitchen CCTV.

450
00:31:01,581 --> 00:31:08,071
You could still secretly recycle food
in a blind spot the camera doesn't reach.

451
00:31:10,408 --> 00:31:12,480
I swear on my name,

452
00:31:12,867 --> 00:31:18,793
I have nothing to be ashamed of,
not in my cooking or my conscience.

453
00:31:19,227 --> 00:31:21,299
I was honest even where no one could see,

454
00:31:21,324 --> 00:31:25,239
and that's why customers
have trusted my cooking.

455
00:31:25,846 --> 00:31:27,613
Yeah, I know.

456
00:31:28,127 --> 00:31:31,388
I can totally vouch that you're clean.

457
00:31:31,427 --> 00:31:37,108
But honestly, kitchen CCTV
can be doctored.

458
00:31:37,133 --> 00:31:40,801
What's that chewed-up pork rind face
babbling about?

459
00:31:40,826 --> 00:31:42,433
From a criminal psychology standpoint,

460
00:31:42,646 --> 00:31:46,926
it's criminals who wave around CCTV,
purchase records, alibis,

461
00:31:46,951 --> 00:31:50,107
and make a huge fuss.

462
00:31:50,387 --> 00:31:55,850
They say people who are really innocent
keep quiet and hold their heads high,

463
00:31:56,015 --> 00:31:59,334
because the truth comes out in the end.

464
00:32:06,320 --> 00:32:08,255
The truth doesn't matter to you people.

465
00:32:08,300 --> 00:32:10,315
What, are you talking down to me?

466
00:32:10,747 --> 00:32:12,675
Talking down is too good
for a guy like you.

467
00:32:12,706 --> 00:32:15,674
- A guy like me?
- Yeah, a guy like you.

468
00:32:17,028 --> 00:32:19,104
You pick a target, spread fake news,

469
00:32:19,129 --> 00:32:21,198
mock them, trample them, destroy them,

470
00:32:21,373 --> 00:32:23,593
and rake in the money,
you lowlife scumbag.

471
00:32:23,618 --> 00:32:24,835
Hey, turn it off. Turn this off now.

472
00:32:24,860 --> 00:32:26,706
You filthy germ, you worm.

473
00:32:26,731 --> 00:32:28,314
(The live stream has ended.
Thank you for watching.)

474
00:32:31,214 --> 00:32:35,676
What? What did Mu Jin do?

475
00:32:36,474 --> 00:32:40,366
I was in class and missed the stream too,
but the comments are completely split.

476
00:32:41,168 --> 00:32:43,915
Half are defending him
and half are criticizing him.

477
00:32:43,961 --> 00:32:47,594
Criticizing him? Why half?

478
00:32:47,935 --> 00:32:50,561
People say that YouTuber's really sketchy.

479
00:32:51,381 --> 00:32:54,962
And that he's harassed people
with fake news more than once or twice.

480
00:32:56,341 --> 00:32:58,249
Can't they tell just by looking at Mu Jin?

481
00:32:59,001 --> 00:33:01,391
Can't they see he's not the type to lie?

482
00:33:01,490 --> 00:33:02,710
Well...

483
00:33:02,756 --> 00:33:07,349
Mu Jin got so mad that during the stream,
he talked down, swore, and made a scene...

484
00:33:08,254 --> 00:33:12,512
Anyway, Jeong Woo's pressing charges,
suing, and digging into everything,

485
00:33:12,537 --> 00:33:13,945
so the culprit should be caught soon.

486
00:33:15,794 --> 00:33:19,660
Jeong Woo's pressing charges and suing?

487
00:33:21,742 --> 00:33:23,248
He's digging into it?

488
00:33:23,273 --> 00:33:26,081
Yeah. He used to be a lawyer.

489
00:33:26,106 --> 00:33:29,727
He says that employee didn't act alone,
that someone was behind it.

490
00:33:29,834 --> 00:33:31,466
He says he'll catch whoever did it soon.

491
00:33:32,381 --> 00:33:34,230
Gyu Rim, I have to get to class.

492
00:33:34,255 --> 00:33:35,803
Okay, I'll call you later.

493
00:33:39,736 --> 00:33:41,356
It was me.

494
00:33:41,749 --> 00:33:45,854
I wanted my son ruined so badly
there'd be nothing left, so I...

495
00:33:45,879 --> 00:33:50,228
I paid those people
and had them do all of it.

496
00:34:01,622 --> 00:34:04,235
"Totally get why you were mad."

497
00:34:05,655 --> 00:34:09,695
"I'd have smacked him
and flipped the whole place."

498
00:34:10,254 --> 00:34:13,241
"Blood rage level is 200 percent."

499
00:34:13,469 --> 00:34:15,715
"Certified master
of digging his own grave."

500
00:34:24,548 --> 00:34:29,599
I had a feeling, but I never thought
you'd actually go on air.

501
00:34:30,035 --> 00:34:33,326
What's with charging in head-on
at every turn?

502
00:34:33,351 --> 00:34:36,281
If you sit still,
people really treat you like a doormat.

503
00:34:40,728 --> 00:34:42,535
I'm a person, not a doormat.

504
00:35:01,274 --> 00:35:05,617
I'd rather see Mu Jin go under.

505
00:35:05,801 --> 00:35:06,994
Pardon?

506
00:35:07,381 --> 00:35:10,589
The poorer he gets, the better for me.

507
00:35:11,848 --> 00:35:13,081
What do you mean?

508
00:35:13,861 --> 00:35:17,752
If Mu Jin can't make money,
I can support him.

509
00:35:20,048 --> 00:35:24,799
Then no one can unfairly accuse me
of not knowing my place and chasing him.

510
00:35:25,240 --> 00:35:29,606
And I won't have to feel
ashamed or humiliated.

511
00:35:30,148 --> 00:35:32,456
I won't have to grovel or feel small,

512
00:35:32,657 --> 00:35:37,884
and I can love him even more proudly.
I couldn't be happier.

513
00:35:42,181 --> 00:35:47,150
If I'd known that a poor woman
loving a conglomerate heir...

514
00:35:48,439 --> 00:35:50,752
would be this miserable,

515
00:35:52,914 --> 00:35:57,373
I'd have run to the ends of the earth
to hide.

516
00:36:00,371 --> 00:36:02,370
But now there's no turning back.

517
00:36:04,168 --> 00:36:06,437
No matter how unfairly I'm misunderstood,

518
00:36:07,344 --> 00:36:10,831
even if I feel so ashamed and humiliated
I want to die...

519
00:36:12,881 --> 00:36:15,878
I won't stop loving Mu Jin.

520
00:36:30,315 --> 00:36:33,104
I'm even going to pray
that he goes broke fast,

521
00:36:35,172 --> 00:36:37,727
so poor, clueless Mu Jin...

522
00:36:39,003 --> 00:36:42,977
Could you please look out for him?

523
00:36:50,694 --> 00:36:52,455
Enjoy your meal.

524
00:37:06,428 --> 00:37:08,913
We're not young anymore.

525
00:37:10,161 --> 00:37:13,835
Live recklessly like that,
and you could be gone in an instant.

526
00:37:14,069 --> 00:37:15,702
Here today, gone tomorrow.

527
00:37:17,401 --> 00:37:21,271
Are you in a bad mood again today?

528
00:37:23,458 --> 00:37:26,454
Want me to show you something again?

529
00:37:27,101 --> 00:37:29,120
Sure.

530
00:37:31,202 --> 00:37:33,920
Okay, Seon. Watch.

531
00:37:34,434 --> 00:37:36,494
A fifty-cent coin. Swoosh.

532
00:37:44,995 --> 00:37:46,335
Ta-da!

533
00:37:47,322 --> 00:37:49,726
- Seok Jung.
- Yeah?

534
00:37:50,564 --> 00:37:52,068
I'm Hong Ok Seon.

535
00:37:53,061 --> 00:37:55,976
We're doing introductions now?
I'm Han Seok Jung.

536
00:37:56,335 --> 00:37:57,638
I'm never wrong.

537
00:37:58,055 --> 00:38:00,615
I've never been wrong once in my life.

538
00:38:00,835 --> 00:38:02,835
I'm always right.

539
00:38:03,534 --> 00:38:09,142
I think that confidence of yours
is really cool. So cool.

540
00:38:09,443 --> 00:38:15,630
In the end, he'll understand
why I had no choice but to do that.

541
00:38:17,584 --> 00:38:20,737
Because he's my child.
Because he's my son.

542
00:38:22,075 --> 00:38:24,227
Is your son giving you a hard time again?

543
00:38:24,828 --> 00:38:26,548
Hey, give me his name and phone number.

544
00:38:26,573 --> 00:38:28,268
I'll meet him and give him an earful.

545
00:38:30,415 --> 00:38:35,643
Anyway, we can't get sick or die.
We have to stay healthy and hang in there.

546
00:38:35,668 --> 00:38:40,394
Like I always say,
once our health goes, it's all over.

547
00:38:41,521 --> 00:38:45,251
And the owner gave you this earlier
for being a regular for ten years.

548
00:38:45,276 --> 00:38:48,878
Don't forget to take that protein.

549
00:38:49,655 --> 00:38:51,715
This?

550
00:38:51,835 --> 00:38:53,781
Yeah. This.

551
00:38:53,894 --> 00:38:56,716
Hey, while we're at it,
have some now. Okay?

552
00:38:59,007 --> 00:39:03,090
Here, you said your arms and legs
have felt weak lately.

553
00:39:03,128 --> 00:39:06,751
My friends drink this all the time too.

554
00:39:07,137 --> 00:39:08,564
I'll make it for you.

555
00:39:13,588 --> 00:39:19,271
Shake it.

556
00:39:19,460 --> 00:39:21,513
Try it. It looks really nutty.

557
00:39:21,864 --> 00:39:26,071
All right. Let's drink it
and get our strength up.

558
00:39:27,585 --> 00:39:29,035
Hey, you have some too.

559
00:39:29,060 --> 00:39:32,180
Sure. Thanks, Ok Seon.

560
00:39:36,272 --> 00:39:39,918
Right. Drink up and get strong,
Hong Ok Seon.

561
00:39:40,054 --> 00:39:42,675
If I were going to fall apart here,
I wouldn't have started.

562
00:39:51,895 --> 00:39:53,687
Enough.

563
00:39:59,287 --> 00:40:00,768
Thanks, Ok Seon.

564
00:40:02,463 --> 00:40:03,810
Here, drink up.

565
00:40:03,835 --> 00:40:07,512
I hear people who watch their figures
drink this a lot these days.

566
00:40:07,659 --> 00:40:10,065
Supposedly it firms you up.

567
00:40:10,395 --> 00:40:13,838
Anyway, at our age,
muscle's what matters most.

568
00:40:14,165 --> 00:40:15,785
Here, let's drink. Cheers.

569
00:40:16,911 --> 00:40:18,075
Cheers.

570
00:40:21,770 --> 00:40:24,427
- Let's drink and get strong, Seon. Okay?
- Okay.

571
00:40:24,452 --> 00:40:25,976
You're the sun.

572
00:40:26,263 --> 00:40:29,290
Your son's sun, and my sun.

573
00:40:29,894 --> 00:40:34,259
Hey, if the sun gets sick and lies down,
the earth is done for.

574
00:40:36,322 --> 00:40:39,408
- Seok Jung.
- Yeah?

575
00:40:40,321 --> 00:40:44,271
Why don't you seem childish to me?

576
00:40:44,961 --> 00:40:48,349
The things you say, the things you do.

577
00:40:49,628 --> 00:40:55,867
In the past, I'd have found it so cringey
and childish that I couldn't stand it.

578
00:40:58,403 --> 00:40:59,521
Why is that?

579
00:41:03,135 --> 00:41:07,264
Why? Do you find me pitiful and cute?

580
00:41:08,289 --> 00:41:12,216
You're in trouble. You've fallen for me.

581
00:41:19,114 --> 00:41:22,460
You said you'd be running the store
yourself starting today, right?

582
00:41:22,701 --> 00:41:24,754
Congratulations, Ko Yun Hui,
on becoming the owner.

583
00:41:25,161 --> 00:41:27,150
You'll do great.

584
00:41:27,388 --> 00:41:29,679
If anything's hard, ask me anytime.

585
00:41:30,068 --> 00:41:34,683
Always supporting
and cheering you on, Jang Hun Tae.

586
00:41:38,951 --> 00:41:42,147
- Ma'am.
- Yes.

587
00:41:42,172 --> 00:41:45,250
- Excuse me.
- Yes, how can I help you?

588
00:41:47,801 --> 00:41:49,271
Yes?

589
00:41:52,422 --> 00:41:54,658
Would you sit down for a moment?

590
00:41:55,641 --> 00:41:58,862
Is something wrong with our food?

591
00:41:58,887 --> 00:42:01,997
No. Nothing's wrong.

592
00:42:02,121 --> 00:42:05,301
The meat's delicious,
and the veggies are super fresh.

593
00:42:06,127 --> 00:42:11,149
I just wanted to talk to you
about something personal.

594
00:42:16,862 --> 00:42:20,722
Have we met before?

595
00:42:21,861 --> 00:42:26,964
You look a little familiar,
but I don't think you're a regular.

596
00:42:32,528 --> 00:42:37,265
It's me, Geum Ju. Lee Geum Ju.

597
00:42:38,334 --> 00:42:42,164
Geum Jeong's younger sister.
Your best friend, Geum Jeong.

598
00:42:43,381 --> 00:42:48,935
I had my reasons,
so I had my whole face redone,

599
00:42:49,088 --> 00:42:50,561
and I changed my name too.

600
00:42:50,794 --> 00:42:53,499
Call me Eun Ok from now on.

601
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:58,602
Through my sister Geum Jeong,

602
00:42:58,896 --> 00:43:04,603
I've been hearing all about Seok Jung
and you in real time.

603
00:43:04,782 --> 00:43:09,720
I heard you remarried a conglomerate guy.

604
00:43:10,428 --> 00:43:15,715
And that your new husband, as kids say,
has got it all.

605
00:43:23,447 --> 00:43:29,935
I know what I did to you
was unforgivable...

606
00:43:32,048 --> 00:43:37,610
but honestly, given how it turned out,
aren't you a little grateful?

607
00:43:45,148 --> 00:43:47,503
Every time lightning struck, I prayed.

608
00:43:49,555 --> 00:43:52,368
That it would strike you.

609
00:43:53,847 --> 00:43:56,044
That you'd have nothing but bad luck.

610
00:43:57,088 --> 00:43:59,842
That you'd be betrayed
by the person you trusted most,

611
00:44:00,796 --> 00:44:04,923
and that the most precious thing you have
would be cruelly taken from you.

612
00:44:07,615 --> 00:44:13,139
That the same thing would happen to you
that happened to me 17 years ago.

613
00:44:16,205 --> 00:44:17,833
Yun Hui.

614
00:44:25,494 --> 00:44:28,199
Looks like they're in the middle
of something serious.

615
00:44:29,181 --> 00:44:34,258
- Right. Let's come back later.
- Okay.

616
00:44:43,641 --> 00:44:46,576
I don't know how you had the nerve
to show your face here,

617
00:44:47,343 --> 00:44:49,783
but today's an important day for me.

618
00:44:53,275 --> 00:44:59,150
Honestly, I'm sick of hating
and sick of being angry.

619
00:45:04,435 --> 00:45:09,072
I just want to forget it all and move on,
so eat quietly and go.

620
00:45:10,295 --> 00:45:12,885
I want to live with Seok Jung again.

621
00:45:16,054 --> 00:45:21,508
I want to grow old and die with him,
with my kids by my side.

622
00:45:26,886 --> 00:45:28,254
Help me, Yun Hui.

623
00:45:28,347 --> 00:45:32,907
Please help me. I'm begging you.

624
00:45:52,709 --> 00:45:54,196
Where's Han Gyu O right now?

625
00:45:55,181 --> 00:45:57,719
My mom really wants to see Han Gyu O.

626
00:45:58,741 --> 00:45:59,993
Where is that jerk?

627
00:46:18,153 --> 00:46:19,328
Ma'am.

628
00:46:21,308 --> 00:46:23,055
Where is Han Gyu O?

629
00:46:25,034 --> 00:46:27,105
I asked you where he is!

630
00:46:30,775 --> 00:46:31,951
I don't know.

631
00:46:32,674 --> 00:46:37,787
You don't know?
You don't even know where your husband is?

632
00:46:38,208 --> 00:46:40,654
I heard you married
that con-artist gigolo.

633
00:46:41,922 --> 00:46:45,683
That you knew he was a criminal
and fooled around with him anyway?

634
00:46:45,762 --> 00:46:47,298
And then you even married him?

635
00:46:47,546 --> 00:46:50,851
A schoolteacher,
who's supposed to set an example?

636
00:46:55,215 --> 00:46:58,113
He's not a criminal.

637
00:47:02,914 --> 00:47:07,357
Does your school know,
with that innocent face of yours?

638
00:47:08,085 --> 00:47:09,788
Do the parents know?

639
00:47:11,240 --> 00:47:16,952
What are growing kids supposed to learn
from a sneaky woman like you?

640
00:47:58,266 --> 00:48:00,251
- We're doing a display, right?
- Yeah.

641
00:48:00,276 --> 00:48:02,616
Which of the two colors do you want?
We have to decide.

642
00:48:03,541 --> 00:48:05,128
I like this color better.

643
00:48:06,835 --> 00:48:08,857
I said pick one of the two.

644
00:48:08,859 --> 00:48:11,588
Why are you picking some random color?

645
00:48:11,613 --> 00:48:12,986
Han Gyu O!

646
00:48:13,881 --> 00:48:15,827
What? What's going on?

647
00:48:18,807 --> 00:48:20,889
Why's your face so white?

648
00:48:21,394 --> 00:48:23,094
And why are your lips so red?

649
00:48:23,340 --> 00:48:26,476
Really? I did my makeup in the dark.

650
00:48:28,145 --> 00:48:30,000
I thought you were a kabuki actor.

651
00:48:30,039 --> 00:48:32,252
Weren't you meeting a friend
from back home today?

652
00:48:33,341 --> 00:48:35,461
I missed you so much I bailed.

653
00:48:35,881 --> 00:48:37,454
Can you hug me?

654
00:48:38,169 --> 00:48:40,953
Wait, here?

655
00:48:41,101 --> 00:48:44,294
Not here. Don't.

656
00:48:49,768 --> 00:48:52,736
Hey, what if customers come in?

657
00:48:52,761 --> 00:48:55,033
Everyone outside is watching.

658
00:48:55,740 --> 00:48:59,180
Hey, are you two going to let go or not?

659
00:49:01,507 --> 00:49:04,719
Are you two trying
to run this business into the ground?

660
00:49:04,874 --> 00:49:07,508
I said let go!

661
00:49:10,548 --> 00:49:15,364
Understood. Anyway, you probably heard
our position from CEO Jeong,

662
00:49:15,845 --> 00:49:19,556
but this is a sham marriage pulled off
by a father and mother with four...

663
00:49:19,581 --> 00:49:21,841
and three fraud priors and their son,
a whole family scheming together.

664
00:49:22,247 --> 00:49:26,350
So we'll go after them for fraud,
extortion, threats, assault,

665
00:49:26,671 --> 00:49:30,327
everything we can file,
civil and criminal, okay?

666
00:49:30,408 --> 00:49:33,454
Don't worry about the cost.
Let's take this all the way.

667
00:49:34,028 --> 00:49:38,777
And they'll definitely bring up
shared responsibility,

668
00:49:38,930 --> 00:49:43,640
and if so, I'll take full responsibility,
so most importantly,

669
00:49:43,667 --> 00:49:47,504
no matter what happens,
keep my Gyu Yeong's name out of it.

670
00:49:47,572 --> 00:49:49,514
Please take special care of that.

671
00:49:49,901 --> 00:49:51,768
- Yes, understood.
- Okay.

672
00:49:52,414 --> 00:49:53,634
Okay.

673
00:49:55,594 --> 00:49:57,634
Ms. Kim Yun Jin is here to see you.

674
00:49:58,921 --> 00:50:00,465
Ms. Kim Yun Jin?

675
00:50:01,965 --> 00:50:03,332
Let's stop here.

676
00:50:08,481 --> 00:50:11,348
Your mom's lost her mind, hasn't she?

677
00:50:12,494 --> 00:50:15,734
She'd go that far
just to get rid of Gyu Rim?

678
00:50:16,493 --> 00:50:21,401
You know once my mom fixates on something,
she's like a car with broken brakes.

679
00:50:21,554 --> 00:50:25,450
Even when she knows she's wrong,
she never stops.

680
00:50:25,475 --> 00:50:27,142
I know. But...

681
00:50:27,170 --> 00:50:28,903
Hey, even if the brakes are broken,

682
00:50:28,905 --> 00:50:30,634
you should at least
hold the steering wheel tight, right?

683
00:50:30,636 --> 00:50:32,041
And steer straight.

684
00:50:32,107 --> 00:50:33,742
Is this the right way?

685
00:50:34,676 --> 00:50:39,019
Only you can stop her, so I came
after thinking it over a hundred times.

686
00:50:39,748 --> 00:50:40,787
I see.

687
00:50:43,034 --> 00:50:46,183
Han Gyu Rim's a really good person.

688
00:50:47,600 --> 00:50:49,451
Even if Mu Jin ends up a beggar,

689
00:50:49,476 --> 00:50:53,264
she'd stand by him. She'd never leave him.

690
00:50:55,360 --> 00:50:56,654
Of course not.

691
00:50:58,163 --> 00:51:00,955
I'm glad at least you see it.

692
00:51:02,041 --> 00:51:06,254
Yes, Gyu Rim's a fine,
upstanding young woman.

693
00:51:07,240 --> 00:51:09,221
There's probably no one else like her.

694
00:51:10,714 --> 00:51:12,640
Sorry to say this in front of you,

695
00:51:13,275 --> 00:51:15,428
but even on a bullet train,
your mom couldn't catch up...

696
00:51:15,453 --> 00:51:18,347
to Gyu Rim's character.

697
00:51:21,241 --> 00:51:23,967
Anyway, thanks for telling me.

698
00:51:25,034 --> 00:51:26,658
Go on, get back to work.

699
00:51:28,139 --> 00:51:29,500
I've got it now.

700
00:51:31,394 --> 00:51:33,704
- All right.
- Please take care of it.

701
00:51:33,729 --> 00:51:36,253
- Sure. I won't see you out.
- Okay.

702
00:51:44,508 --> 00:51:45,967
Hong Ok Seon...

703
00:51:47,049 --> 00:51:49,447
Are you really trying to take me on?

704
00:52:01,635 --> 00:52:04,848
(Wando Red Sea Bream Capellini Pasta)

705
00:52:10,286 --> 00:52:12,953
(Gyu Rim)

706
00:52:14,340 --> 00:52:15,493
Hello?

707
00:52:26,341 --> 00:52:27,934
No customers, Gyu Rim.

708
00:52:28,368 --> 00:52:29,921
Not a single one.

709
00:52:33,167 --> 00:52:36,247
I think we're really going under.

710
00:52:38,007 --> 00:52:40,233
There's plenty of time before closing.

711
00:52:40,508 --> 00:52:42,269
People might still come late.

712
00:52:44,808 --> 00:52:49,254
Until I contact you,
don't send any abalone for a while.

713
00:52:50,295 --> 00:52:53,253
Nothing's wrong.

714
00:52:53,881 --> 00:52:57,633
And if you need people at our farm,

715
00:52:57,658 --> 00:53:00,537
just let me know.

716
00:53:01,671 --> 00:53:07,868
There are two guys here
who are about to be out of work.

717
00:53:13,206 --> 00:53:18,275
I'm a little busy right now,
so I'll call you back later.

718
00:53:18,401 --> 00:53:20,922
Go feed the dogs, Mom.

719
00:53:21,777 --> 00:53:22,908
Okay.

720
00:53:38,055 --> 00:53:40,228
Why do you keep sighing?

721
00:53:42,441 --> 00:53:47,054
How'd it go meeting Han Gyu Yeong?

722
00:53:47,774 --> 00:53:49,696
Took you long enough to ask.

723
00:53:49,782 --> 00:53:51,986
Wasn't that why you wanted to see me?

724
00:53:52,011 --> 00:53:53,623
Defying your bride-to-be's strict orders?

725
00:53:53,648 --> 00:53:55,734
She's not my bride-to-be yet.

726
00:53:56,027 --> 00:54:00,844
Hey, even if things are over
between you and Mu Jin,

727
00:54:01,094 --> 00:54:06,081
how can you cut him off so coldly,
like you couldn't care less?

728
00:54:06,620 --> 00:54:09,474
Why do you keep changing the subject?

729
00:54:09,499 --> 00:54:12,290
Why bring up Mu Jin
when we're talking about Han Gyu Yeong?

730
00:54:12,366 --> 00:54:13,567
Because of Han Gyu Rim?

731
00:54:13,741 --> 00:54:15,407
Don't you even watch the news?

732
00:54:15,694 --> 00:54:17,667
Haven't you heard anything
about our restaurant?

733
00:54:17,848 --> 00:54:19,774
What? What news?

734
00:54:19,799 --> 00:54:23,546
Doesn't it strike you as odd...

735
00:54:23,571 --> 00:54:25,911
that I'm here with you at this busy hour?

736
00:54:27,167 --> 00:54:29,001
How can you be so clueless?

737
00:54:30,381 --> 00:54:34,021
Seriously, why aren't you busy?

738
00:55:00,834 --> 00:55:04,901
Chef, someone just called
to make a reservation.

739
00:55:04,934 --> 00:55:08,074
They'll be here in 20 minutes.

740
00:55:08,207 --> 00:55:11,554
Twenty plus one.
Twenty-one people are coming.

741
00:55:12,647 --> 00:55:14,894
- Now?
- Yes, now.

742
00:55:19,108 --> 00:55:21,544
- Got it.
- Okay. You've got this.

743
00:55:25,901 --> 00:55:30,409
Really? Okay. I'll hurry.

744
00:55:36,668 --> 00:55:38,241
You don't have anything to do, right?

745
00:55:41,387 --> 00:55:43,309
- Really?
- Yeah.

746
00:55:44,280 --> 00:55:47,180
But Mu Jin's the only one in the kitchen.

747
00:55:47,299 --> 00:55:51,393
Our temporary assistant chef left early
since we figured there'd be no customers.

748
00:55:54,040 --> 00:55:58,184
I'll come. I'm coming now. Okay.

749
00:56:09,680 --> 00:56:11,500
Let me help you.

750
00:56:12,580 --> 00:56:14,200
Excuse me.

751
00:56:15,394 --> 00:56:17,174
You buttoned it wrong.

752
00:56:17,507 --> 00:56:18,987
There.

753
00:56:19,488 --> 00:56:22,674
- Thank you.
- Not at all. I'm counting on you.

754
00:56:22,874 --> 00:56:26,545
- I'm counting on you.
- Not at all.

755
00:56:34,701 --> 00:56:36,934
Everything the Chairman said was right.

756
00:56:38,388 --> 00:56:42,088
What right do you have
to boss him around like that?

757
00:56:42,734 --> 00:56:44,654
What, does he owe you something?

758
00:56:46,996 --> 00:56:51,827
If I were him, I wouldn't have given
someone like you the time of day.

759
00:56:56,716 --> 00:57:01,148
You must be starving. Eat first.

760
00:57:01,521 --> 00:57:03,922
Carbs give you room to breathe,

761
00:57:03,947 --> 00:57:06,195
and good character. Haven't you heard?

762
00:57:06,601 --> 00:57:09,193
- I can't hear you.
- What?

763
00:57:11,320 --> 00:57:14,771
I can't hear anything right now,
so stop nagging and eat.

764
00:57:14,796 --> 00:57:16,475
I don't think I can do that.

765
00:57:16,834 --> 00:57:20,889
The nagging continues
until you become a decent person.

766
00:57:20,914 --> 00:57:23,128
Until your eardrums are about to burst.

767
00:57:24,581 --> 00:57:28,529
Right. Did Gyu Seo go to the hospital?

768
00:57:34,681 --> 00:57:37,247
Hello, Gyu Seo.

769
00:57:38,228 --> 00:57:40,234
Did you go to the ENT
and get a full checkup?

770
00:57:41,514 --> 00:57:43,529
You didn't go, did you?

771
00:57:46,075 --> 00:57:49,115
They said your eardrum ruptured,

772
00:57:49,198 --> 00:57:52,839
so you need to get a proper exam
and get treated or have surgery,

773
00:57:52,864 --> 00:57:54,961
don't you, you punk?

774
00:57:55,121 --> 00:57:56,908
I went to the hospital.

775
00:57:57,088 --> 00:57:58,961
They said nothing's wrong. I'm fine.

776
00:57:59,248 --> 00:58:01,054
Don't worry too much, Heung Sik.

777
00:58:01,321 --> 00:58:04,774
I think you're lying.

778
00:58:05,721 --> 00:58:08,827
How can you be fine
after your ear bled like that?

779
00:58:09,208 --> 00:58:11,768
First thing tomorrow morning,
go to the hospital and...

780
00:58:12,942 --> 00:58:15,396
Meet me at the playground Gyeol likes
in ten minutes.

781
00:58:15,588 --> 00:58:17,181
If you don't come, you're dead.

782
00:58:17,368 --> 00:58:18,648
What are you doing?

783
00:58:30,589 --> 00:58:31,781
Why are you overreacting?

784
00:58:34,441 --> 00:58:36,692
Who are you to overreact
about someone else's business?

785
00:58:37,381 --> 00:58:40,818
Is that any way to talk to your brother
who got hurt saving you?

786
00:58:40,843 --> 00:58:42,970
Brother? Who's my brother?

787
00:58:43,134 --> 00:58:45,401
Why'd you do something pointless
that I never asked you to do?

788
00:58:47,308 --> 00:58:49,341
I don't think it was pointless.

789
00:58:49,467 --> 00:58:50,467
What?

790
00:58:52,100 --> 00:58:54,456
Even if I went back to that moment,

791
00:58:55,057 --> 00:58:57,027
I'd run over and save you again,
Gyu Yeong.

792
00:58:57,052 --> 00:58:59,770
- Hey.
- Even beaten to death, I'd save you.

793
00:59:00,861 --> 00:59:03,274
Who do you think you are?

794
00:59:03,299 --> 00:59:05,617
Why are you making me feel pathetic too?

795
00:59:05,781 --> 00:59:09,067
I already feel like I'm about to lose it.
Why are you driving me crazy?

796
00:59:33,528 --> 00:59:37,141
What are you, an ostrich?
You think hiding your head is enough?

797
00:59:41,660 --> 00:59:42,734
Why are you crying?

798
00:59:43,394 --> 00:59:44,927
Because your pink eye hurts?

799
00:59:45,562 --> 00:59:48,475
Pink eye doesn't hurt. My eye does.

800
00:59:50,574 --> 00:59:53,367
Anyway, why are you crying?
You're breaking my heart.

801
00:59:54,828 --> 00:59:56,221
What am I, anyway?

802
00:59:56,980 --> 00:59:58,753
What kind of person am I?

803
01:00:02,541 --> 01:00:04,067
Are you asking me?

804
01:00:05,234 --> 01:00:07,721
Why am I such a softie for a guy?

805
01:00:08,768 --> 01:00:10,574
Am I soft tofu like Gyu Min says?

806
01:00:10,599 --> 01:00:12,039
The ultimate sucker?

807
01:00:12,188 --> 01:00:14,335
Don't I have any pride or backbone?

808
01:00:16,441 --> 01:00:19,387
If you don't know yourself,
how would I know you?

809
01:00:20,309 --> 01:00:24,021
Don't cry, kid.
Why's a grown man crying at night?

810
01:00:24,521 --> 01:00:28,174
Hey, a man only cries
three times in his life.

811
01:00:28,209 --> 01:00:32,289
Exactly. So why am I crying right now?

812
01:00:33,360 --> 01:00:35,640
Is this even worth crying over?

813
01:00:35,761 --> 01:00:37,961
This isn't something to cry about.

814
01:00:38,461 --> 01:00:41,735
What's wrong with me all of a sudden?
This is driving me crazy.

815
01:00:44,087 --> 01:00:47,160
I thought puberty ended
back in eighth grade.

816
01:00:47,934 --> 01:00:51,881
Hey, are you going through menopause?

817
01:01:00,422 --> 01:01:03,769
- Yep, menopause.
- Just go, please.

818
01:01:09,257 --> 01:01:10,668
It's menopause.

819
01:01:18,867 --> 01:01:20,207
Okay.

820
01:01:20,294 --> 01:01:21,528
Welcome.

821
01:01:23,156 --> 01:01:25,523
- Gyu Min?
- Yes. Please come in.

822
01:01:25,548 --> 01:01:28,200
- I even skipped dinner for this.
- Good.

823
01:01:29,574 --> 01:01:30,688
Dad?

824
01:01:30,713 --> 01:01:31,884
Yeah, go on in.

825
01:01:36,321 --> 01:01:37,601
What are you doing here?

826
01:02:02,739 --> 01:02:03,849
Mu Jin.

827
01:02:05,217 --> 01:02:08,500
- The booking was Chairman Jang Hun Tae.
- What?

828
01:02:08,607 --> 01:02:11,667
He brought along all the biggest names
among F&B chairmen.

829
01:02:12,934 --> 01:02:16,610
Those chairmen post restaurant reviews
on social media all the time,

830
01:02:16,787 --> 01:02:18,304
and they're known for being picky eaters.

831
01:02:18,306 --> 01:02:21,781
Did they come to kill us or to save us?

832
01:02:25,134 --> 01:02:26,527
They came to save us.

833
01:02:48,213 --> 01:02:50,587
Gyu Min, I'm on my way now.

834
01:02:50,715 --> 01:02:52,036
It'll take about ten minutes.

835
01:02:52,576 --> 01:02:54,676
Okay, see you soon.

836
01:03:57,544 --> 01:03:59,577
(Love on the Menu)

837
01:03:59,602 --> 01:04:03,014
I'll take your family down
one by one instead.

838
01:04:03,039 --> 01:04:05,531
I've cut ties with all of them,
so what family do I have?

839
01:04:05,556 --> 01:04:07,642
Who are you to meddle
in my family business?

840
01:04:07,681 --> 01:04:09,681
It's not someone else's business.
It's my daughter's.

841
01:04:09,683 --> 01:04:11,254
- Gyu Rim is my daughter.
- What?

842
01:04:11,279 --> 01:04:13,390
Yes. It's true that we got married, but...

843
01:04:13,415 --> 01:04:15,860
- What jerk posted this?
- That's not true...

844
01:04:15,885 --> 01:04:18,160
Gyu Rim. What happened to you?

845
01:04:18,185 --> 01:04:19,581
Gyu Yeong, Gyu O.

846
01:04:19,606 --> 01:04:22,593
I'll drag Mu Jin down to rock bottom.

847
01:04:22,694 --> 01:04:24,397
I'll make him come back.

848
01:04:25,563 --> 01:04:27,363
Dramaday.me
